Input: every binding of the aggregate rule's body over COMPLETE lower strata (DA.14b runs the body plan once at all levels), projected to [group cols.., aggregated cols..] with each binding's level (max over its body atoms) and height. Steps: (1) sort by (projected row, level, height) and dedup by projected row keeping the best level and lowest height - one binding is one derivation, the best wins; (2) group by the leading `group` columns (sorted, so groups are contiguous); (3) per op over the group's DISTINCT aggregated tuples: count = number of distinct tuples (count(x, y) counts distinct pairs); min / max over one variable by `cmp` (DA.14b passes ValueTable::cmp_rendered, so node values order by render key, checkout-stable); sum over one variable with checked i64 addition - a non-Int value or an overflow is RulesError::Type naming `pred` (`sum over a non-integer value in `weight/2``, `sum overflows i64 in ..`); (4) each output row: group values, then results interned as Int (count / sum) or the min / max handle, reordered to the head's column order; level = the WEAKEST level among the group's tuples (Q5); height = 1 + max height. Empty input yields no rows (count is never 0 - absence is a negation; documented). Output order: sorted by group handles (internal; rows() re-sorts by rendered values).

