Variants: for each rule, one variant per delta-capable body literal i (a positive relation atom of this stratum, a lower-stratum / EDB atom, or a `tiered` builtin) - literals j < i read Src::Old, i reads Src::Delta, j > i read Src::All (the standard semi-naive assignment by literal index, independent of the join order), plus the variant `delta: None` (everything All) used only in the first round of the first level. Order: sips_order (DA.5b) with `first = i` when literal i is a relation atom (the delta is the smallest input), sizes known for EDB and lower strata (the stratum is planned just before it runs, so lower relations are complete), ties to source order. A positive atom becomes Scan when nothing is bound, else Lookup on the index whose permutation lists the bound columns first in column order, then the rest; constants are bound columns; a repeated variable inside one atom becomes a `checks` entry. Index requests across all variants are collected, sorted and deduplicated per predicate (identity always present). Negation: Neg on the index keyed by the atom's bound columns (wildcards must be the trailing columns of some permutation - the planner requests that permutation). Hoist: at a `reaches` literal whose source (X, or Y when only Y is bound - a backward walk) is bound, the planner computes live = variables used by later steps or the head; if no variable bound by the preceding steps is live (X itself included) AND every preceding literal reads complete input (EDB, a lower stratum or a builtin - never an atom of the stratum being planned), the preceding steps become `ReachMulti.seed` (run to completion to collect distinct seeds with their best level), followed by one levelled BFS and the remaining steps with `bind` set - R1's 3.3 ms shape; the composite counts as one delta-capable tiered literal for the variant assignment (its rows of level L are new input in level L's first round). Otherwise a per-binding Reach (memoised per source by DA.11), which is also wha