A depth-first walk over `steps` with one bindings array (u16-indexed handles, a trail to undo on backtrack) - an explicit step-index loop, not recursion per step. Per step: Scan / Lookup read Relation cursors with the View its Src selects at the mode's level L (Old: levels 0..=L stable runs, plus levels < L when this is a later level's first round; Delta: level L recent; All: 0..=L) - the exact mapping is the one the levelled loop in DA.14b states, and Explain adds max_height; `checks` compare repeated variables. Neg: !exists_prefix over ALL levels (Q5: negation reads the complete lower relation, adds no tier). Cmp: Eq / Ne compare handles; the `<` family through ValueTable::cmp_values, Node operands by rendered key; mixed types are false. Assign binds. Call: a domain or string builtin through Builtin::call with ValueRef args, its rows interned and memoised per (builtin, bound handles) in `memo` (a Lookup, never iterated); an Err(msg) becomes RulesError::Builtin{name: "<name>/<arity>", message}; scc calls read the relation DA.14b materialised from Closure::scc_rows. Reach: Closure::reach per binding (memoised there), rows filtered to tier <= L, each row's tier joining the binding level. ReachMulti: the first time it runs in an evaluation it executes its seed steps (complete inputs only, DA.10's hoist condition) to collect the distinct seeds with their best level, calls Closure::reach_from once, and fills MultiState (kept for explain, DA.15); later calls read MultiState.rows by Src at level L. Binding level = max over positive rows' tiers (builtin rows carry theirs; node / attribute rows FACT); height = max over IDB rows' heights. Eval mode: every complete binding goes to `emit`, which DA.14b uses to push head rows; each emitted binding adds 1 to budget.used and memo / closure rows add theirs; when used > cap, `tripped` is set and run_body returns Ok early (DA.14b turns it into RulesError::Budget with the head's name and line). Explain mode: no budget; `lits` carries every literal's instantiation for DA.15's candidate choice. No HashMap iteration; single-threaded.

