    merged: &'a MergedGraph,
    loc: Loc<'a>,                       // enum Loc { Owned(Box<Locator<'a>>), Borrowed(&'a Locator<'a>) }
    first: HashMap<NodeId, (usize, usize)>, // node -> (graph, node index): first graph naming it, built once O(V)
    files: OnceCell<HashMap<NodeId, Option<String>>>,
    projects: OnceCell<HashMap<NodeId, String>>, // PROJECT node -> its repo-relative path
    scopes: RefCell<BTreeMap<String, Rc<HashSet<NodeId>>>>,
    loaded: RefCell<Vec<&'static str>>,  // attribute columns materialised, in load order (tests + marker)
}
impl<'a> CodeFacts<'a> {
    pub fn new(merged: &'a MergedGraph) -> Self;
    pub fn with_locator(merged: &'a MergedGraph, loc: &'a Locator<'a>) -> Self;
    pub fn locator(&self) -> &Locator<'a>;
    /// Check's strict membership; `scope` resolved through answers::resolve_scope (a label works).
    pub fn members(&self, scope: &str) -> Rc<HashSet<NodeId>>;
    pub fn loaded_attributes(&self) -> Vec<&'static str>;
    pub(crate) fn files(&self) -> &HashMap<NodeId, Option<String>>;
    pub(crate) fn projects(&self) -> &HashMap<NodeId, String>;
}
```
GraphSource: node_ids = MergedGraph's node order with later duplicates dropped (the first graph naming an id wins, as check's Ctx::new and the Locator do); edges = all_edges order. FactSource (method names as DA lands the trait, R1 §2.2): tables() = &CODE_PROFILE.tables (registry names come from CODE_TABLES.registries); render_node(id) = the node's qname from the first graph's nav (the checkout-stable key rows sort by), `(unknown:<id>)` for an id no graph names (Locator::locate's spelling); node_kind / node_cells from the first graph naming the id (`first`), so one id in several language graphs is one node; attributes() = CODE_ATTRIBUTES, each materialised only when DA asks for its rows, in node_ids order: `qname/2` Str and `name/2` Str (nav), `file/2` Str and `line/2` Int (Locator::locate: the 1-based line; an unlocated node has no row), `repo/2` Str (`repo#<k>`: k = the 0-based position of the node's RepoId among the distinct RepoIds of merged.graphs in order, so the first repo given is repo#0 and --with repos follow; checkout-stable, unlike the path-derived RepoId bits), `project/2` Str (the label of the PROJECT whose path is the longest segment prefix of the node's file, or the PROJECT's own label), `parent/2` Node (nav.parent_of), `role/2` Str (node_kind::name of each graph::roles::roles_in kind), `origin/2` Str (the ORIGIN cell's `provenance`, e.g. external, test_fixture, nav_route). Each load pushes its name onto `loaded` and prints `[rules] facts attr=<name> rows=<n>` once per CodeFacts. edge_tier(e) = edge_tier_of(e) = tier_of(Evidence::of(e).as_ref(), e).0 mapped fact -> Tier::Fact, derived -> Derived, heuristic -> Heuristic (one rule for why, check and the rules layer). builtins(): `in_scope(N, Scope)` - modes (bound, bound) filter and (free, bound) generator in node order over members(resolve_scope(merged, Scope)), the resolution memoised per distinct string (so a project label or `project:<path>` qname works in a rule, as every `--scope` flag accepts; a path with a PROJECT at it wins); a scope no node sits in yields nothing (check pre-validates its own scopes, DB.3a); `under(Path, Prefix)` - (bound, bound) filter over two strings, both normalised like check's norm_path (strip leading `./` / `/`, trailing `/`; `.` and empty mean the root and hold every path; segment boundary, `web` does not hold `webhooks/x`). members(path): LITERAL, check's Ctx::members exactly - the union of nodes whose `files()` entry is under `path` (answers::in_scope, segment boundary) and PROJECTs whose `projects()` path is; no label resolution (check's scopes arrive resolved); memoised per string. The builtins hold an Rc of CodeFacts' inner state (files, projects, scope cache), so `builtins()` can hand out `&dyn Builtin` without borrowing self mutably. located_edge(loc, from, category, to, ev, (tier, note)) -> ViolationEdge: the row at the EVIDENCE site (0-based line + 1) when it names a file, else at `from`'s Locator location - the body of check's Ctx::row, which DB.3a switches to it. Everything iterates Vecs / node order; HashMaps are looked up only.
