DESIGN: parsers extract, the graph resolves. The parser records what the AST says about each binding's type in the one carrier the generic receiver pass already reads (CodeNav::local_types, LA.35a: innermost-first before field_types, a recorded local bypasses the bare-field gate, `""` = a local of unknown type that shadows a same-named field, a `self.<f>` type aliases field f), so no graph code changes and every TS-family file (TS / JS / React / Angular / Vue go through this parser) gains it at once; Dart / Solidity / Terraform have their own parsers. A binding's scope is the node its calls are attributed to (`from` of collect_calls_in): a method, a function, a function field, a call-initialised field (CH.2) or, for top-level expression statements, the MODULE. Nested arrow / function-expression bodies share that node (collect_calls_in descends into them), so their parameters and locals are recorded there too; nested function_declaration / method_definition / class bodies stay skipped as today.
Alternatives weighed: (a) graph-side typing: the graph holds no AST. (b) Record only class-typed bindings and drop the unknown ones: binds more where TS callbacks collapse into one scope (a describe-level `let store: S` beside an it-level `const store = make()`), but guesses: `const api = makeOther(); api.fetch()` in one callback would bind another callback's ApiService. LA.35a's contract (CodeNav::record_local_type: first type, a later different type -> "", order-independent) is kept; measured cost (file-level regex spec052/probe/DF/df22/scripts/conflicts.py, an over-count since methods are separate scopes): class-typed call sites on a name also bound untyped / differently in the file: mem0 322 of 598 (mostly module-level test code), wpf 19 / 249, shell 56 / 171, kina 57 / 129 (largely the `inject()` locals this packet types), nestjs 1 / 95. (c) Type call-result locals (`const s = make()` with `make(): S`) through return annotations: needs CodeNav::return_types read by the generic receiver pass (only Go's hook reads it, CA.2a) - a gap, not this item. (d) Block scoping (`let` / `const` per block): a call site names only its enclosing callable, so no scope can be narrower than that.
1. record_param_types(func, src, scope, acc): params = func.child_by_field_name("parameters") (formal_parameters); an arrow without parens has field `parameter` (an identifier) -> record_local(scope, name, "", Param). For each named child of kind required_parameter | optional_parameter: pattern = child_by_field_name("pattern"): an `identifier` -> ty = child_by_field_name("type").and_then(|t| annotated_class_type(t, src)).unwrap_or("") (annotated_class_type already maps `ns.Foo` / `Foo<T>` / `Foo | null` / `Foo | undefined` to `Foo` and primitives, arrays, tuples, function / object / literal types and multi-type unions to None); kind `this` -> skip; any other pattern (object_pattern, array_pattern, rest_pattern, assignment_pattern) -> "" for every identifier / shorthand_property_identifier_pattern inside it (the binds_name walk). Constructor parameter properties (`private api: ApiService`) are recorded as constructor locals of the same type their field_types entry has, so A6.2b's constructor binds are unchanged.
2. record_local(acc, scope, name, ty, src_kind): acc.nav.record_local_type(scope, name, ty); when ty is non-empty, acc.local_src.entry((scope, name.to_string())).or_insert(src_kind) (the first source of an agreed type; read only by the marker).
3. record_declarator_type(decl, src, scope, acc), decl a variable_declarator: name = child_by_field_name("name"); an `identifier` -> (i) child_by_field_name("type") -> annotated_class_type (Annotated; `let s: Store;` with no value included); else value = child_by_field_name("value"): (ii) new_expression -> its `constructor`: identifier text / member_expression's `property` text (`new ns.Widget<T>()` -> Widget), kept only when its first char is ASCII uppercase (New), else ""; (iii) as_expression -> its type child through class_type_name (Annotated); (iv) member_expression whose `object` kind is `this` and `property` kind is property_identifier / private_property_identifier -> "self.<p>" (Alias; receiver_type reads it as field p); (v) call_expression whose `function` is an identifier and whose first argument is an identifier with an ASCII-uppercase first char -> push LocalInject { scope, name, callee, ty } and record nothing yet; (vi) anything else (a call result, a literal, an await, a chain) -> "". A pattern name (object / array pattern) -> "" per identifier.
4. collect_calls_in, in its node loop before the descent: `"variable_declarator" => record_declarator_type(node, src, from, acc)`, `"arrow_function" | "function_expression" => record_param_types(node, src, from, acc)`, `"for_in_statement"` -> "" for each identifier of its `left`, `"catch_clause"` -> "" for each identifier of its `parameter`. lexical_declaration / variable_declaration need no arm: their declarator children are visited by the same loop.
5. visit_method (methods, the constructor and accessors), visit_function_field (its arrow / function value), emit_function, emit_function_value: record_param_types(<callable node>, src, <its id>, acc) right before collect_calls_in. visit_abstract_method has no body and records nothing.
6. parse_file_stats, after the visit loop (every import statement of the file is read by then): let gate = inject_import_bindings(&acc.imports); for each LocalInject in push order: record_local(scope, name, if gate.contains(callee) { ty } else { "" }, Inject) - the same `inject` import gate A6.2b applies to `inject(T)` fields (InjectFnCandidate). Then LocalStats: over acc.unresolved, every CallQualifier::Attribute{base, ..} site whose base is in acc.nav.local_types[from]: a non-empty type counts `typed` and its local_src kind, "" counts `unknown`. Print, when typed > 0: `[ts-locals] typed receivers=<n> (param=<p> annotated=<a> new=<w> inject=<i> alias=<s>) unknown=<u> file=<file>` (the per-file convention of `[ts-state]` / `[ts-fields]` / `[ts-abstract]`). parse_file_stats returns (FileParse, FnFieldStats, AbstractStats, StateFieldStats, LocalStats, ReceiverGateStats, EndpointArgStats): LocalStats goes between StateFieldStats and ReceiverGateStats so the existing test destructurings (`(.., stats)`, `(parse, .., gate, _)`, `(parse, .., gate, args)`, `(_, _, _, stats, ..)`, `(_, stats, ..)`, `(_, _, stats, ..)`) keep their meaning.
7. No graph change. resolve_calls binds the site through resolve_via_receiver_type (EVIDENCE graph:calls rule receiver_type at the call's line, LC.3b; recv_stats counts it under typescript). The endpoint extractor and CH.3c's receiver gate (field_new_types) are untouched.
TESTS. parsers/code/typescript/src/lib.rs mod tests (helper `local_types(parse, qname) -> BTreeMap<String, String>`): (a) params_and_locals_record_their_types - `import { Repo } from './repo';
