1. RPC_CALLS note, appended: '; an EVM contract call (ethers / hardhat / TypeChain / viem / wagmi / web3.js in TypeScript, go-ethereum and abigen bindings in Go) pairs to a Solidity external / public function or public getter of the build only through: the contract named at the site (a hardhat factory, getContractAt / deployContract name, a `<C>__factory` or a `<C>.sol/<C>.json` artifact: derived); the ABI the client is built with (an ABI of two or more entries every one of which exactly one concrete contract declares, itself or through an in-repo base: derived; an ABI entry the contract only inherits from a base outside the build, such as OpenZeppelin `balanceOf` / `owner`, identifies no contract); or, with no usable ABI, a receiver or ABI name equal to exactly one contract name (heuristic). It never pairs on the function name alone, and a call whose ABI variants name two contracts pairs nothing. Not read: a contract binding made in another file than its calls; a method name built at run time or passed through a wrapper in another file; an ABI imported through a tsconfig alias or a package; a `.json` ABI that is no hardhat / foundry artifact.'
